<title>HONG KONG: HK to tender HK$500 mln five-year exchange notes.</title>
<headline>HK to tender HK$500 mln five-year exchange notes.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-06-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Hong Kong Monetary Authority said on Friday it would tender its twelfth issue of five-year Exchange Fund Notes on June 17.</p>
<p>The HK$500 million notes carry a coupon of 6.55 percent per annum, with interest payable semi-annually in arrears.</p>
<p>The notes will mature on June 17, 2002.</p>
<p>An additional HK$100 million will be held as reserves by the HKMA for supply to market makers in the secondary market.</p>
<p>Settlement will take place on June 17, 1997, the HKMA said.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6441. http://www.hk97.com</p>
